## json-schema-org/JSON-Schema-Test-Suite — `optional/format/`

The `Rule.format` assertions (`email`, `uri`, `uri_reference`, `uuid`, `ipv4`,
`ipv6`, `hostname`, `date`, `time`, `date_time`, `duration`, `json_pointer`)
are anchored against the official corpus published at
https://github.com/json-schema-org/JSON-Schema-Test-Suite, pinned at commit
`be54236db6e8e6bb2e098ed16fb4c61e73f5a9ac` (2026-08, `tests/draft2020-12/`):

  * vendored verbatim under `src/testdata/json-schema-test-suite/optional/format/`
    (12 files — every `optional/format/*.json` file whose `format` value is
    one this module implements)
  * driven mechanically by `src/json_schema_format_vectors.zig` (one entry
    per file, `@embedFile`d) and `src/json_schema_format_test.zig` (the
    runner, both directions — `valid: true` must pass and `valid: false`
    must be rejected)

This module implements JSON Schema 2020-12's `format` VOCABULARY (a set of
independent string-shape assertions), not the full JSON Schema document
model (`type`/`properties`/`$ref`/`allOf`/etc. composition) — its `Rule`
struct is this module's own vocabulary, only modeled after JSON Schema's
keyword semantics (see this module's `README.md` `Provenance:` statement and
root.zig's module doc). So only the
`format`-keyword sub-corpus is in scope; the main per-keyword suite
(`tests/draft2020-12/*.json`, outside `optional/`) tests a document model this
module does not have and is not vendored.

Not vendored, deliberately: `optional/format/idn-email.json`,
`idn-hostname.json`, `iri.json`, `iri-reference.json`, `uri-template.json`,
`relative-json-pointer.json`, `regex.json`, `ecmascript-regex.json`,
`unknown.json` — formats this module's `Format` enum does not implement (see
json_schema_format_vectors.zig's doc comment and the "vendored file count
matches expectation" canary in json_schema_format_test.zig).

Within the vendored files, `json_schema_format_test.zig`'s `group_skips` /
`case_skips` name specific corpus material outside this module's documented
subset (with a reason each, counted by a canary, never silently dropped):
the "A-label (punycode) host names" group in `hostname.json` (IDNA/Unicode
BIDI semantic validation, not RFC 1123 label shape); five `email.json` cases
requiring a quoted-string local part or a domain address-literal (`isEmail`'s
documented "practical RFC 5321 subset"); the `uri.json` authority-shape
(userinfo/port) cases (`isUri`'s documented "not a full parser: component
splitting and authority shape are out of scope"); and the `time.json` /
`date-time.json` leap-second-outside-23:59 and offset-optional cases (both
pre-existing, documented `isTime` design choices — see root.zig).

